---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Facility Operations, Readings & Logs, PPM — Fusionedge">
<article class="am am-v2">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Public+Sans:ital,wght@0,400..800;1,400..800&display=swap">

  <p class="am-back"><a href="/#usecases-title">Use cases</a></p>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <div class="am-hero">
    <div class="am-hero-top">
      <h1 class="am-h1">Facility Operations, Readings &amp; Logs, PPM</h1>
      <p class="am-lead">A fast-growing co-working operator had no clear view of what was happening across its campuses.</p>
      <p class="am-sub">FusionEdge gave every campus the same processes, tracked 32,000+ assets, and measured electricity by time of day so tenants are billed for what they use.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="am-kpis">
      <div><strong>14 campuses</strong><span>in 6 cities on one standard way of working</span></div>
      <div><strong>32,000+</strong><span>assets tracked</span></div>
      <div><strong>−45%</strong><span>unplanned breakdowns</span></div>
      <div><strong>10 weeks</strong><span>rollout time</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Results -->
  <p class="am-eyebrow">Measure twice. Cut once.</p>
  <h2 class="am-h2 am-center">The results, at a glance</h2>

  <div class="am-box am-glance">
    <div class="am-col">
      <h3 class="am-h3">PPM tasks done on time</h3>
      <p class="am-cap">Share of planned maintenance completed on schedule</p>
      <div class="am-hb am-n"><span>Before</span><div class="am-t"><i class="am-g" style="width:52%"></i></div><b>52%</b></div>
      <div class="am-hb am-n"><span>After · with photo proof</span><div class="am-t"><i class="am-ok" style="width:96%"></i></div><b>96%</b></div>
      <p class="am-foot">45% fewer unplanned breakdowns.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="am-col">
      <h3 class="am-h3">Cleaning checklist compliance</h3>
      <p class="am-cap">Share of checklists completed, all campuses</p>
      <div class="am-vb" role="img" aria-label="Compliance rose from 61% to 95%">
        <div><b>61%</b><i class="am-g" style="height:61%"></i><span>Before</span></div>
        <div><b>95%</b><i class="am-ok" style="height:95%"></i><span>After</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="am-foot">The same schedule at every campus.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="am-col">
      <h3 class="am-h3">Electricity cost recovered</h3>
      <p class="am-cap">Extra-hours power now billed to the right tenant</p>
      <svg class="am-ring" viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="18% more electricity cost recovered">
        <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="44" fill="none" stroke="#f1efea" stroke-width="10"/>
        <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="44" fill="none" stroke="#2e9e62" stroke-width="10" pathLength="100" stroke-dasharray="18 82" transform="rotate(-90 60 60)" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <text x="60" y="67" text-anchor="middle">+18%</text>
      </svg>
      <p class="am-foot">Overall energy cost down 12%.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="am-box am-found">
    <h3 class="am-h3">What we found</h3>
    <p class="am-cap">Across the 14 campuses, before FusionEdge</p>
    <div class="am-hb am-n"><span>Meter readings taken on paper</span><div class="am-t"><i class="am-bad" style="width:100%"></i></div><b>100%</b></div>
    <div class="am-hb am-n"><span>Cleaning checklists completed</span><div class="am-t"><i class="am-warn" style="width:61%"></i></div><b>61%</b></div>
    <div class="am-hb am-n"><span>PPM tasks done on time</span><div class="am-t"><i class="am-warn" style="width:52%"></i></div><b>52%</b></div>
    <div class="am-hb am-n"><span>Breakdowns reported to the central team</span><div class="am-t"><i class="am-bad" style="width:33%"></i></div><b>1 in 3</b></div>
    <div class="am-hb am-n"><span>Tenant power after 9 pm that was billed</span><div class="am-t"><i class="am-bad" style="width:0.7%;min-width:4px"></i></div><b>0%</b></div>
  </div>

  <!-- Story -->
  <div class="am-story">
  <section class="am-sec">
    <div class="am-sec-head">
      <p class="am-kicker">01 · Context</p>
      <h2 class="am-h2">The client and the challenge</h2>
      <div class="am-facts">
        <div><strong>14</strong><span>campuses across 6 cities</span></div>
        <div><strong>0</strong><span>single SOP across campuses</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="am-sec-body">
      <p>The client runs co-working spaces across India. Tenants pay for a space that simply works: clean desks, cool air, working lifts, and steady power. Delivering that every day needs visibility of what is happening at every campus, reliability of every AC, DG set, lift, and pump, and a record of who did what and when so costs can be controlled.</p>
      <p>The client had none of these across its campuses. As it opened new locations, equipment broke down and the central team often did not know. Each campus had its own cleaning schedule and its own way of working. There was no single SOP, and electricity used by tenants after office hours was not measured, so the operator paid for it.</p>
      <p>The operator wanted every campus, old and new, to work the same way before it expanded further.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="am-sec am-rev">
    <div class="am-sec-head">
      <p class="am-kicker">02 · Findings</p>
      <h2 class="am-h2">What we found</h2>
      <div class="am-facts">
        <div><strong>1 in 3</strong><span>breakdowns reached the central team</span></div>
        <div><strong>0%</strong><span>of after-9 pm tenant power billed</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="am-sec-body">
      <ul class="am-list">
        <li><b>14 different cleaning and maintenance routines.</b> Every campus worked its own way.</li>
        <li><b>52% of PPM tasks were done on time.</b> Almost half of planned maintenance was late or missed.</li>
        <li><b>1 in 3 breakdowns was reported to the central team.</b> Most issues were fixed, or not, without anyone knowing.</li>
        <li><b>100% of meter readings were taken on paper.</b> There was no live view of electricity use.</li>
        <li><b>0% of tenant power use after 9 pm was billed.</b> Extra-hours electricity was a hidden loss.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="am-sec">
    <div class="am-sec-head">
      <p class="am-kicker">03 · Approach</p>
      <h2 class="am-h2">The solution</h2>
      <div class="am-facts">
        <div><strong>10 weeks</strong><span>to roll out to all campuses</span></div>
        <div><strong>5 days</strong><span>to set up a new campus</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="am-sec-body">
      <p>FusionEdge was rolled out to all 14 campuses in 10 weeks, in four steps.</p>
      <ol class="am-ol">
        <li><b>One standard for every campus.</b> The same SOPs, cleaning schedules, and digital checklists were set up across all campuses. A new campus now goes live in 5 days using the same template.</li>
        <li><b>Every asset on one system.</b> 32,000+ assets, including ACs, DG sets, UPS, lifts, and pumps, were added with their service history.</li>
        <li><b>PPM that actually happens.</b> Planned maintenance schedules were loaded for every asset. Technicians get reminders on their phone, and each task is closed with a photo as proof.</li>
        <li><b>Electricity tracked by time of day.</b> Using Readings &amp; Logs, meters are read at set times, including the 9 am to 9 pm working window. The operator can see which tenant used how much power, and when, and bill extra-hours use correctly.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
  </div>

  <h2 class="am-h2">Before and after</h2>
  <div class="am-box am-tw"><table class="am-table">
    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Before</th><th>After</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>How campuses work</th><td data-l="Before">14 different routines</td><td data-l="After">One standard SOP</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Breakdowns</th><td data-l="Before">Often unknown to the central team</td><td data-l="After">Every breakdown logged and tracked, with 45% fewer</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Planned maintenance</th><td data-l="Before">52% done on time</td><td data-l="After">96% done on time with photo proof</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Cleaning</th><td data-l="Before">Different schedules, 61% checklist compliance</td><td data-l="After">Same schedule everywhere, 95% compliance</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Electricity readings</th><td data-l="Before">On paper, once a day or less</td><td data-l="After">Digital readings at fixed times through the day</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Extra-hours power</th><td data-l="Before">Not measured and not billed</td><td data-l="After">Measured and billed to the right tenant</td></tr>
      <tr><th>New campus setup</th><td data-l="Before">About 3 weeks</td><td data-l="After">5 days</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="am-note">Spotting energy spikes early, and fixing the equipment behind them, cut overall energy cost by 12%.</p>

  <h2 class="am-h2">The five outcomes</h2>
  <div class="am-rows">
    <div><em>01</em><b>Standardization</b><p>All 14 campuses follow the same SOPs, cleaning schedules, and checklists.</p><strong>14</strong></div>
    <div><em>02</em><b>Savings</b><p>18% more electricity cost recovered from tenants, and 12% lower energy bills.</p><strong>+18%</strong></div>
    <div><em>03</em><b>Energy insight</b><p>A live view of power use by time of day, with spikes flagged early.</p><strong>24h</strong></div>
    <div><em>04</em><b>Reliable PPM</b><p>96% of planned maintenance done on time, and 45% fewer breakdowns.</p><strong>96%</strong></div>
    <div><em>05</em><b>Evidence and quality</b><p>Every task is closed with a photo and time stamp, so service quality can be proven to tenants.</p><strong>100%</strong></div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="am-h2">Modules used</h2>
  <div class="am-mods">
    <div><b>Asset Management</b><p>Every asset and its service history.</p></div>
    <div><b>Preventive Maintenance</b><p>PPM schedules with reminders and photo proof.</p></div>
    <div><b>Readings &amp; Logs</b><p>Electricity and equipment readings at set times.</p></div>
    <div><b>Digital Checklists</b><p>The same cleaning and SOP checklists at every campus.</p></div>
    <div><b>Executive Dashboard</b><p>One view of all campuses.</p></div>
  </div>
</article>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Container matches the nav: same max width + side padding so the left edge lines up with the logo.
     If your header uses different values, change these two variables only. */
  .am{--wrap:1610px;--pad:clamp(20px,4vw,40px);
    --fg:#1b1530;--mut:#6c6780;--line:#e9e6ee;--ok:#2e9e62;--bad:#cf4a3c;--warn:#e58f35;--g:#e5e1d8;
    font-family:"Public Sans",sans-serif;box-sizing:border-box;
    width:100%;max-width:calc(var(--wrap) + var(--pad) * 2);margin:0 auto;padding:16px var(--pad) 96px;
    color:var(--fg);font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;overflow-wrap:break-word}
  .am *,.am *::before,.am *::after{box-sizing:border-box;font-family:"Public Sans",sans-serif}
  .am svg text{font-family:"Public Sans",sans-serif}
  .am p{margin:0 0 14px;max-width:none}

  .am-back{margin:0 0 14px!important}
  .am-back a{font-size:13px;color:var(--mut);text-decoration:none}
  .am-back a:hover{color:#5b1f6e}

  .am-h1,.am-h2{font-style:italic;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--fg);text-align:left}
  .am-h2{font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,28px);line-height:1.25;margin:72px 0 16px}
  .am-center{text-align:center;margin:0 0 28px}
  .am-h3{font-size:14.5px;font-weight:600;margin:0;line-height:1.35}

  /* Hero */
  .am-hero{display:block;width:100%;border-radius:20px;overflow:hidden;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#f6f1e1 0%,#fbf8ef 60%,#fff 100%)}
  .am-hero-top{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1.3fr) minmax(0,.9fr);gap:clamp(24px,4vw,56px);align-items:start;padding:clamp(32px,5vw,64px) clamp(20px,3vw,40px)}
  .am-h1{font-size:clamp(30px,3.6vw,48px);line-height:1.1;margin:0;max-width:9em}
  .am .am-lead{font-size:clamp(17px,1.7vw,22px);line-height:1.45;color:var(--mut);margin:0}
  .am .am-sub{font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;margin:0}

  .am-kpis{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);background:#fff}
  .am-kpis div{padding:22px clamp(14px,2vw,40px)}
  .am-kpis div+div{border-left:1px solid var(--line)}
  .am-kpis strong{display:block;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,32px);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.01em;line-height:1.2}
  .am-kpis span{display:block;font-size:13px;color:var(--mut);margin-top:6px;line-height:1.45}

  .am .am-eyebrow{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin:56px 0 18px;font:10px "Public Sans",sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--mut)}
  .am-eyebrow::before,.am-eyebrow::after{content:"";flex:1;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}

  /* Boxes */
  .am-box{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:#fff}
  .am .am-cap{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--mut);margin:2px 0 16px;line-height:1.4}
  .am .am-foot{font-size:13px;font-weight:500;margin:auto 0 0;padding-top:20px}

  .am-glance{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}
  .am-col{padding:22px clamp(16px,2vw,28px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0}
  .am-col+.am-col{border-left:1px solid var(--line)}

  .am-hb{display:grid;gap:6px;font-size:12.5px;margin-bottom:16px}
  .am-n{grid-template-columns:1fr auto;column-gap:12px;align-items:center}
  .am-n span{grid-column:1/-1}
  .am-hb b{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:500;min-width:40px;text-align:right}
  .am-t{height:12px;display:flex}
  .am-t i{display:block;height:100%;border-radius:3px}
  .am-col .am-t{background:#f1efea;border-radius:3px}
  .am-g{background:var(--g)}.am-ok{background:var(--ok)}.am-bad{background:var(--bad)}.am-warn{background:var(--warn)}

  .am-vb{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;gap:20px;height:130px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);margin:8px 0 24px}
  .am-vb div{width:64px;height:100%;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;align-items:center;position:relative}
  .am-vb b{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:4px}
  .am-vb i{display:block;width:100%;border-radius:2px 2px 0 0}
  .am-vb span{position:absolute;bottom:-22px;font-size:12px;color:var(--mut)}
  .am-ring{width:110px;align-self:center;margin:6px 0}
  .am-ring text{font-size:20px;font-weight:500;fill:var(--fg)}

  .am-found{margin-top:12px;padding:22px clamp(16px,2vw,28px) 8px}

  /* Prose — kept to a readable line length, left edge stays aligned */
  .am-story{margin-top:96px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .am-sec{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1.6fr);gap:clamp(32px,6vw,96px);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,96px) 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .am-sec-head{align-self:start;position:sticky;top:96px}
  .am-sec-head .am-h2{margin:0 0 28px}
  .am .am-kicker{font:600 11px "Public Sans",sans-serif;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5b1f6e;margin:0 0 12px}
  .am-facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px 24px}
  .am-facts strong{display:block;font-size:clamp(24px,2.4vw,32px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;line-height:1.15;color:#5b1f6e}
  .am-facts span{display:block;font-size:13px;color:var(--mut);margin-top:4px;line-height:1.45}
  .am-sec-body{font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.75;max-width:760px}
  .am-sec-body p{margin:0 0 20px}
  .am-sec-body p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
  .am-ol{list-style:none;margin:8px 0 0;padding:0;counter-reset:s;display:grid;gap:0}
  .am-ol li{counter-increment:s;position:relative;padding:20px 0 20px 48px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .am-ol li::before{content:counter(s,decimal-leading-zero);position:absolute;left:0;top:24px;font:600 13px "Public Sans",sans-serif;color:#5b1f6e}

  /* Table */
  .am-tw{overflow-x:auto}
  .am-table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}
  .am-table th,.am-table td{text-align:left;padding:14px 16px;vertical-align:top;border:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .am-table tbody tr:last-child>*{border-bottom:0}
  .am-table thead th{font-size:12px;font-weight:500;color:var(--mut)}
  .am-table tbody th{width:24%;font-weight:600}
  .am .am-note{font-size:13px;color:var(--mut);margin:10px 0 0}

  /* Outcomes */
  .am-oc{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-left:1px solid var(--line)}
  .am-oc div{padding:18px clamp(14px,2vw,24px) 20px;border-right:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .am-oc b{display:block;font-size:14.5px}
  .am-oc p{font-size:13px;color:var(--mut);margin:4px 0 0!important;line-height:1.55}

  /* ---------- Responsive ---------- */
  @media (max-width:1024px){
    .am-hero-top{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1.2fr)}
    .am-h1{grid-column:1/-1;max-width:none}
  }
  @media (max-width:760px){
    .am-hero-top{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px}
    .am-kpis{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
    .am-kpis div:nth-child(3){border-left:0}
    .am-kpis div:nth-child(n+3){border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .am-glance{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .am-col+.am-col{border-left:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .am-oc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}
    .am-h2{margin-top:56px}
    .am-story{margin-top:64px}
    .am-sec{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px;padding:48px 0}
    .am-sec-head{position:static}
    .am-sec-body{font-size:15.5px}
  }
  @media (max-width:540px){
    .am-oc{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .am-table,.am-table tbody,.am-table tr,.am-table th,.am-table td{display:block;width:100%!important}
    .am-table thead{display:none}
    .am-table tbody tr{padding:12px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .am-table tbody tr:last-child{border-bottom:0}
    .am-table tbody th,.am-table td{border:0;padding:3px 0}
    .am-table td::before{content:attr(data-l) ": ";color:var(--mut)}
  }
  .am-list{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}
  .am-list li{position:relative;padding:16px 0 16px 22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .am-list li:first-child{border-top:0;padding-top:0}
  .am-list li::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;top:27px;width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--bad)}
  .am-list li:first-child::before{top:11px}
  .am-mods{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,minmax(0,1fr));border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-left:1px solid var(--line)}
  .am-mods div{padding:18px clamp(14px,2vw,24px) 20px;border-right:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .am-mods b{display:block;font-size:14.5px;color:#5b1f6e}
  .am-mods p{font-size:13px;color:var(--mut);margin:4px 0 0!important;line-height:1.55}
  @media (max-width:1024px){.am-mods{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}
  @media (max-width:760px){.am-mods{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}
  @media (max-width:540px){.am-mods{grid-template-columns:1fr}}

  /* ---- v2 layout tweaks (this page only) ---- */
  .am-v2 .am-hero{background:linear-gradient(180deg,#efe9f5 0%,#f7f3fa 60%,#fff 100%)}
  .am-v2 .am-hero-top{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.3fr) minmax(0,1fr);row-gap:28px}
  .am-v2 .am-h1{grid-column:1/-1;max-width:16em}
  .am-v2 .am-glance{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.2fr) minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr)}
  .am-v2 .am-found{margin-top:24px}
  .am-v2 .am-rev .am-sec-head{order:2}
  .am-v2 .am-rev{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.6fr) minmax(0,1fr)}
  .am-v2 .am-rev .am-sec-body{justify-self:start}
  .am-rows{border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .am-rows div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:56px minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,2fr) 120px;gap:24px;align-items:baseline;padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .am-rows em{font-style:normal;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#5b1f6e}
  .am-rows b{font-size:17px}
  .am-rows p{margin:0!important;color:var(--mut);font-size:15px}
  .am-rows strong{text-align:right;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,28px);font-weight:600;color:#2e9e62;letter-spacing:-.02em}
  @media (max-width:1024px){.am-v2 .am-glance{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}
  @media (max-width:760px){
    .am-v2 .am-hero-top{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .am-v2 .am-glance{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .am-v2 .am-rev{grid-template-columns:1fr}
    .am-v2 .am-rev .am-sec-head{order:0}
    .am-rows div{grid-template-columns:40px minmax(0,1fr) auto;gap:6px 16px}
    .am-rows p{grid-column:2/-1;grid-row:2}
    .am-rows strong{grid-column:3;grid-row:1}
  }
</style>